Vendor behavior before this tweak:

1. QCFG replies were accepted when they merely contained OK and any +QCFG line.
2. A reply belonging to another simultaneous AT request could therefore be parsed
   as a transport mismatch and trigger AT+CFUN=1,1.
3. One ping sample without "64 bytes" triggered AT+CFUN=1 and ifup cellular.
4. Any malformed QNETDEVCTL reply was treated as a stopped data call.

The full pre-change worker is archived at:
tweaks/cellular_worker_single_instance_fix/changed/usr/sbin/cellular/quectel_rm500u
